{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nw4EcNNpLLAnKqguQN7Drk","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/attest/specs/229/spec.md b/attest/specs/229/spec.md\nindex c0932a4..83392bc 100644\n--- a/attest/specs/229/spec.md\n+++ b/attest/specs/229/spec.md\n@@ -10,11 +10,11 @@ The gate reads the commit. Each iteration's criteria, selected tests and tenant\n \n An empty iteration is told so. When an iteration ends with `HEAD` equal to `start_sha`, the gate runs (on the approved tree, where the criteria already fail), the log and the feedback both carry \"you committed nothing: no commit since <start>; N path(s) modified or untracked in the working tree, which the gate does not read\" and \"commit your work; the gate reads the commit, not the tree\", and the loop continues. An executor that answers `done` before committing on its first iteration and commits on its second passes as before (`test_an_empty_iteration_is_fed_back_and_a_later_commit_passes`).\n \n-An empty build is halted. When the last iteration ends with `HEAD` equal to `start_sha`, the record is `halted` with a new stop class `empty`, provenance `executor`, detail \"the executor committed nothing; ...\" with the count of paths left in the tree. The class is the executor's, so counsel reads it and a steer retries it under R3; no new family. `STOP_CLASSES` and the build and verify schemas carry `empty` (build/9, verify/8). The status can never be `pass` with `sha` equal to `start_sha`.\n+An empty build is halted. A build is empty when the tree its record names is the approved tree outside `paths.records`: `git diff --quiet <approval sha> HEAD -- . ':!<records>'` finds nothing. The comparison is against the approval, not the attempt's own `start_sha`, so a retried attempt whose head already carries a prior attempt's valid commits adopts them and owes no commit of its own; an attempt that ends on the approved tree, whatever it left in the working directory, is what #227 was. When the last iteration ends empty, the record is `halted` with a new stop class `empty`, provenance `executor`, detail \"the executor committed nothing; ...\" with the count of paths left in the tree; an earlier empty iteration is fed back and the loop continues. The class is the executor's, so counsel reads it and a steer retries it under R3; no new family. `STOP_CLASSES` and the build and verify schemas carry `empty` (build/9, verify/8). The status can never be `pass` on the approved tree.\n \n-Verify refuses an empty build. A passing build record whose `sha` equals its `start_sha` is refused before any adapter runs: \"the latest build record names no change (sha equals start_sha ...); nothing to review\". The build no longer writes such a record; the refusal is verify's own guard against any record shaped this way, whoever wrote it.\n+Verify refuses an empty build. A passing build record whose tree is the approved tree outside `paths.records` is refused before any adapter runs: \"the latest build record names no change; nothing to review\". The build no longer writes such a record; the refusal is verify's own guard against any record shaped this way, whoever wrote it.\n \n-The doctor's seventh proof: no attested item is empty. For every merged, fully-staged item, the passing build's `sha` is not its `start_sha`. `[doctor].built_since` names a commit at or before which merges are before the window: named on every run, never failed, so #227 stands on the record as the specimen and the tenant is not red forever. Absent, the window is proof three's. A build record with no `start_sha` (written before the field) is counted as not readable, not failed. This repository declares `built_since = \"dae6d765f3d6\"`, #227's merge. The proof's test is dogfood like the other five and is deselected from `[tests].run` and the CI test job the same way; the doctor job runs it.\n+The doctor's seventh proof: no attested item is empty. For every merged, fully-staged item, the passing build's tree differs from the approved tree outside `paths.records`. `[doctor].built_since` names a commit at or before which merges are before the window: named on every run, never failed, so #227 stands on the record as the specimen and the tenant is not red forever. Absent, the window is proof three's. A build record whose approval cannot be resolved is counted as not readable, not failed. This repository declares `built_since = \"dae6d765f3d6\"`, #227's merge. The proof's test is dogfood like the other five and is deselected from `[tests].run` and the CI test job the same way; the doctor job runs it.\n \n Not in this item: re-doing #227's change (its own item, filed on this product once merged); a ruling record voiding an attestation (R4); reading records from `HEAD` in every stage (R5); an executor-side change to the adapter (the instruction already says commit and stop; a mechanism is what was missing, not a sentence).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec2614fd-fe76-497e-a0f4-348a6650b419","uuid":"59036bc9-c6d5-4fb8-b2a5-eb2e7d4c587b","timestamp":"2026-09-27T15:35:23.367Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"diff --git a/attest/specs/229/spec.md b/attest/specs/229/spec.md\nindex c0932a4..83392bc 100644\n--- a/attest/specs/229/spec.md\n+++ b/attest/specs/229/spec.md\n@@ -10,11 +10,11 @@ The gate reads the commit. Each iteration's criteria, selected tests and tenant\n \n An empty iteration is told so. When an iteration ends with `HEAD` equal to `start_sha`, the gate runs (on the approved tree, where the criteria already fail), the log and the feedback both carry \"you committed nothing: no commit since <start>; N path(s) modified or untracked in the working tree, which the gate does not read\" and \"commit your work; the gate reads the commit, not the tree\", and the loop continues. An executor that answers `done` before committing on its first iteration and commits on its second passes as before (`test_an_empty_iteration_is_fed_back_and_a_l